That doesn't seem to be the way it's working now, at least as regards
the Challenges (that might be intentional and I'd probably even agree
with it, though we planned a bunch of our strategy around it :) ; also,
I don't see where going from birdie with bells on to double top would
get you fewer points unless getting one achievement made others go away,
which wasn't the case last year. Actually, looking back, it was the case
that if you had a Birdie, you didn't have a Dilithium Star, but if you
had a hat trick and a birdie with bells on, you got both. (Actually,
sawtooth got credit for Grand Slam, Hat Trick, Double Top w/Bells,
and Birdie w/Bells, _but not the Dilithium Star._ Counterintuitive.)

In my opinion --- and it's not my party --- any achievement you get
shouldn't go away. If you get a gold star and then get a dilithium star,
that's still two different achievements in two separate games. The
birdie and so on should be the same way. However, I think you should
only be able to get _one_ of each type of streak, though you can get
another one with Bells. Otherwise you could alternate genders and just
keep picking up birdies. On the other hand, with the KoL challenge 
worth as much as an ascension, maybe multiple ascensions do need to be
overvalued.

(And you can get bells by being careful with multiple servers, anyway,
so how much they should be worth is debatable...)

